questions.passage_md:
The Sunrise School library keeps one dictionary per book in the binary file `library.dat`:

```text
{"id": 11, "title": "Kite Days", "copies": 2}
{"id": 12, "title": "Salt Roads", "copies": 0}
{"id": 13, "title": "Night Train", "copies": 1}
```

A student volunteer wrote this function to issue a book:

```python
import pickle
def issue(book_id):
    recs = []
    with open("library.dat", "rb") as f:
        try:
            while True:
                recs.append(pickle.load(f))
        except EOFError:
            pass
    for r in recs:
        if r["id"] == book_id and r["copies"] > 0:
            r["copies"] -= 1
    with open("library.dat", "wb") as f:
        for r in recs:
            pickle.dump(r, f)
```

